# Force LF on checkout for every text file, on every platform. Without `eol=lf`, `* text=auto` writes the
# platform-native ending on checkout, so a Windows checkout gets CRLF in 322 of the skill files even with
# core.autocrlf=false; a consumer that vendors the skills by copying that checkout then commits CRLF (#129,
# ADR-0090). The repo's blobs are already LF; this only changes what a working-tree checkout receives.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.mjs text
# Shell scripts must check out with LF even on Windows, or the bash that runs them
# (CI and the ADR/ruleset gate tests) fails on CR bytes (`$'\r': command not found`).
*.sh text eol=lf

# No merge drivers here, on purpose (ADR-0108, superseding ADR-0087). GitHub ignores merge drivers when it
# decides whether a pull request conflicts, and a local override of a driver name can silently drop lines. The
# files every PR used to append to (the review log, the receipt log, the BDD coverage log, the changelog) are now
# directories of one file per change, so two PRs add two different files and there is nothing to merge.

# The pre-push hook template is a shebang script; it must check out with LF so it runs under the shell
# that git invokes it with, even on Windows.
.claude/skills/bootstrap/templates/pre-push text eol=lf

# This repo's OWN armed hooks (self-dogfood, ADR-0053) are shebang scripts git invokes directly, so they
# must check out with LF even on Windows or the shell fails on the CR bytes.
.githooks/pre-push text eol=lf
.githooks/install-hooks.mjs text eol=lf
.claude/skills/bootstrap/templates/install-hooks.mjs text eol=lf
